+Implement the next feature in the existing Local AI React/Tauri application.
+
+FEATURE:
+Dynamic LM Studio model selector.
+
+IMPORTANT:
+- Do NOT redesign the UI.
+- Do NOT modify App.css.
+- Do NOT modify Tauri files.
+- Do NOT modify src/services/ai.ts unless absolutely required.
+- Preserve the existing working chat functionality.
+- Preserve the existing three-panel UI.
+
+Use the existing getModels() function from:
+src/services/ai.ts
+
+Requirements:
+
+1. When App starts, call getModels().
+2. Store the returned models in React state.
+3. Set the first available model as the default selected model.
+4. The top-bar model selector must display the selected model.
+5. Clicking the model selector should show a dropdown containing all models returned by LM Studio.
+6. Selecting a model must update selectedModel.
+7. New chat messages must use the currently selected model.
+8. Show a small loading state while models are being loaded.
+9. If model loading fails, keep the current hardcoded model as fallback:
+   qwen/qwen3.5-9b
+10. Do not break the existing chat API.
+11. Do not add mock models.
+
+After implementation run:
+
+npm run build
+
+Fix all TypeScript errors until the build succeeds.
+
+Then briefly explain which parts of App.tsx were changed.

